think With red #73 closed by mantra/spool.rye, the next Lindy-first crux is the layer provenance and Tablecloth actually need: a name over a large artifact. Tablecloth names one-resin artifacts; the spool handles large ones; nothing yet bound a human name to a whole spool.
think Confirmed the import path: Zig's lazy analysis means spool.rye's selftest @embedFile decls are not analyzed when only its pub functions/consts are referenced, so pond/apps/spool_cloth.rye imports mantra/spool.rye cleanly (symlinked pond/apps/mantra/spool.rye) without needing corpora symlinks in that dir — verified with a throwaway probe.
think Designed spool_cloth.rye as Tablecloth's sibling: a LargeCatalog binds a name to a whole spool (its ordered resin recipe), store_large winds via spool.spool_content, fetch_large unspools by name. Bounded max_large_artifacts small (4) on purpose — each entry owns a ~33 KB spool, so the catalog is heavy by design; four named large artifacts is ample for the naming crux and the memory cost is named in the source.
